From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:01:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: pci-apple-ans: Add the T8011 host

The A10X (T8011) storage port carries the same ANS NVMe controller as the
A10's, with the same L1 substate control and the same stop over system
sleep: match it with the T8010's host data.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/pci/0044; matched on "apple,t8011-pcie" with the
 T8010 data instead of a J120 host; the bring-up write limits (read-only
 namespaces except namespace 1, no discard, admin command allow-list, no
 APST) and their nvme core quirks dropped, so the controller is handled as
 on the A10 iPads.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c b/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c
index 53efee55a..cc631b7dd 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c
@@ -108,6 +108,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id nvme_pci_apple_ans_hosts[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,s8000-pcie", .data = &apple_ans_host_s8003 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,s8003-pcie", .data = &apple_ans_host_s8003 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8010-pcie", .data = &apple_ans_host_t8010 },
+	/* The A10X storage port carries the A10's ANS controller. */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t8011-pcie", .data = &apple_ans_host_t8010 },
 	{ }
 };
 
